<title>USA: Pratt to buy Interturbine flight repair.</title>
<headline>Pratt to buy Interturbine flight repair.</headline>
<dateline>EAST HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jet engine maker Pratt &amp; Whitney, a unit of United Technologies Corp., said Thursday it has agreed to buy NV Interturbine's flight repair group, with operations in Dallas and Singapore.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Pratt said in a statement the move will enhance its growing worldwide customer support network. The acquisition will be completed in about two months.</p>
<p>Interturbine is a privately held company based in the Netherlands.</p>
<p>((--Hartford newsroom, (860) 727-0224))</p>
